# ============================================================
# plan: warm_soak -- pump down, soak warm, return to air
# ============================================================
# The first thermal vacuum test: the platen and shroud held at 40 °C for 30
# minutes under rough vacuum. No cold, so no liquid nitrogen.
#
# Start: ambient. The chamber at atmosphere with its door closed, the platen and
#   shroud between 10 and 40 °C.
# End:   at atmosphere, the vent valve open. Both zones off, both pumps off.
# Fails: the chamber is not at atmosphere at the start, does not reach 5 Torr
#   within 20 minutes, a zone does not reach 40 °C within 60 minutes, or the
#   chamber does not return to air as vent_to_ambient requires.
#
# Takes about 1 hour 40 minutes: 6 to pump down, up to 60 to warm, 30 to soak.

load rLACO
record every 10 s

begin at ambient
pumpdown to 5 Torr
warm to 40 C within 60 min
hold 30 min

hvc platen off
hvc shroud off
vent within 60 min
log soaked at 40 C and back at atmosphere
